 This is the **default protocol** for every noctusai engineer dispatch. Briefs are expected to be ≤50 lines and reference this doc. Anything not overridden in the brief applies as written here.
 
+## 0a. Auto-mode safety discipline — SURFACE, never bypass (READ FIRST)
+
+You operate in **auto-mode** (no human-prompt loop). This is your safety contract — match every command against the forbidden catalog BEFORE acting. Bypassing autonomously is **forbidden**; the right move is **STOP + surface + return blocked**. Depth: `KB § PATTERNS/common/background-engineer-safety-discipline.md`.
+
+**Forbidden action catalog** (match here BEFORE running):
+- `git push --no-verify` / `git commit --no-verify` (engineers never commit either way — but never `--no-verify` even if briefly authorized to commit)
+- `git push --force` / `git push -f` / `git push --force-with-lease`
+- `git push origin <branch>:dev` / `:main` / `:prod` without **per-action authorization in the brief**
+- `git reset --hard`
+- `git branch -D` on non-engineer-own branches
+- `rm -rf` on shared paths (repo root, `.claude/cache/`, primary tree's `node_modules` / `.venv`)
+- Any `--force` / `--force-rebuild` / `--force-purge` on platform tools (`noctus.dev.*` / `noctus.vps.*` / deploy)
+- Bypassing secrets / auth / permission gates (plaintext creds, `chmod +x` to skip a guard, disabling a hook)
+
+**Carve-out** — `git reset --soft HEAD^` to undo your own over-broad `git add` before re-staging scoped IS allowed (recovery, not destructive). `--no-verify` is allowed ONLY when the brief explicitly authorizes it with a written rationale (engineer-seed §2 KB-autostage-hook shape) — silence in the brief = forbidden.
+
+**The surface protocol — 4 steps:**
+
+```
+1. STOP     stop in place. Do NOT run the proposed bypass.
+2. SURFACE  noctus.dev.surface_to_tech_lead(
+              reason=<one-line>,
+              proposal_md=<filled template — see KB doc>,
+              current_state_md=<git diff --cached --name-only + pwd>,
+              attempted_resolution_md=<what you tried>)
+            Print the returned exit_marker_msg as your FINAL output line and stop.
+3. RETURN   status=blocked. The exit_marker_msg IS your return (encodes surface_id
+            + worktree path + the blocked command).
+4. WAIT     Tech-lead responds via noctus.dev.respond_and_resume then
+            noctus.dev.dispatch_resume_brief — do not proceed until re-dispatched.
+```
+
+**Why this rule exists.** N≥4 recurrence in the 2026-05-29 session (8-way promotion + noc-graph lazy-rebuild + extractor-correctness + W2 component_bundle each took a destructive shortcut autonomously). Auto-mode gave them no human gate; this rule + this section IS the gate. The tech-lead carries the conversational context with the user, sees the broad picture (peer activity, cross-product impact, what the user authorizes), and routes the bypass decision. Your worktree-local view doesn't see it. The `surface_to_tech_lead` tool makes the round-trip ergonomic — one call, not a manual proposal file.
+
+**Anti-patterns** — "the bypass was small / harmless" · "the hook failure was a false-positive" · "I'll silently bypass + log it in the return note" · "the brief didn't explicitly forbid this specific bypass" · "this is the only way to make progress" · "the surface round-trip costs too much" — all cases route through STOP + surface + return blocked, never autonomous bypass. Depth + worked examples + composes-with at the KB pointer above.
+
